    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. honestly though, a lot of this feels like typical NIMBY stuff that just holds back progress. how do people usually justify these arguments when they're actually being looked at from a serious urban planning perspective? like, are these concerns actually based on anything substantial or are they just excuses to keep things the way they are?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
